---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../../components/SectionHeading.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Quality & Inspection" description="Learn how Belaro Precision reviews drawing requirements, tolerances and inspection for CNC machined parts and coordinated secondary processes.">
  <Header />
  <main>
    <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">QUALITY APPROACH</span><h1>Quality begins with<br/><em>clear requirements.</em></h1><p>Inspection expectations should be understood before production begins—not after parts are made.</p></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="container"><SectionHeading eyebrow="OUR APPROACH" title="A practical, drawing-led quality process" text="Inspection methods and records are agreed according to part geometry, critical dimensions and customer requirements."/><div class="quality-steps"><article><b>01</b><h3>Drawing review</h3><p>Identify critical dimensions, geometric requirements, material specifications and revision status.</p></article><article><b>02</b><h3>Process consideration</h3><p>Review the relationship between part geometry, machining process, tolerance and inspection method.</p></article><article><b>03</b><h3>Dimensional inspection</h3><p>Check agreed dimensions using suitable measuring equipment and documented criteria.</p></article><article><b>04</b><h3>Records & communication</h3><p>Confirm the inspection records or reports required for the order before production starts.</p></article></div></div></section>
    <section class="quality-band"><div class="container quality-band-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">TOLERANCE CAPABILITY</span><h2>Accuracy depends on<br/><em>the part and the process.</em></h2><p>Typical achievable tolerances may be in the ±0.01–0.02 mm range on suitable features. Final capability must be confirmed after reviewing dimensions, material, geometry, machining setup, temperature and measurement conditions.</p></div><div class="quality-stat"><strong>±0.01–0.02</strong><span>mm*</span><p>*Indicative capability only. Not a blanket guarantee for every dimension or component.</p></div></div></section>
    <section class="section section-soft"><div class="container"><SectionHeading eyebrow="PROJECT DOCUMENTATION" title="Agree the evidence your project needs" text="Inspection reports, material documentation and other quality records should be confirmed during quotation. Availability depends on the agreed scope and supply chain."/><div class="note-card"><strong>Important</strong><p>Belaro does not claim certifications, accredited laboratory status or specific inspection equipment on this website. Please request confirmation of the documentation and measurement capability required for your part.</p></div></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="container intro-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">SUPPLIER-NETWORK QUALITY</span><h2>Keep secondary processes inside the <em>agreed quality scope.</em></h2></div><div><p class="lead">When grinding, heat treatment or surface finishing is coordinated through the Dongguan supplier network, the required specification and evidence should be defined before production.</p><p>Tell us which dimensions apply after processing, which surfaces must be masked, and whether hardness, finish, coating or supplier records are required. Availability and inspection scope are confirmed per project.</p><a class="text-link" href="/services/secondary-processes/">Secondary process requirements <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div></section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
